Z||000001||Fierowrecker||05-20-2001||08:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shianne:<BR><B>Has anyone tried setting the timeing ahead by a couple of degrees on the 2.5's  I have heard this will increase the power??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Shianne!<BR>Don't bother advancing the base timing, as the computer will retard it back when running...<BR>The starting of the car might be a little harder too, as the base timing being advanced affects the way the car starts...<BR>Better to find someone to reprogram a chip for you, but it really isn't worth the bother as the 2.5L doesn't have any extra power to give you...<BR>The 2.5L is an econo engine, better to put in a 3800 V6...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
